    48	```python
    49	def reference_azimuth(md: Dict[str, object], eps: float = 1e-6):
    50	    """Scene-intrinsic reference azimuth (float tensor-scalar) or None.
    51	
    52	    EXACTLY the rule cylindrical_pose_features has always applied: target
    53	    source azimuth; degenerate source -> azimuth of the largest-r pose among
    54	    {source, context_poses}; all-degenerate -> None. Extracted so the
    55	    cylindrical and target_frame paths cannot drift; cylindrical_pose_features
    56	    is refactored to call this (behavior pinned by the existing
    57	    test_invariant_conditioning suite, which must stay green untouched).
    58	    """
    59	    ...
    60	
    61	def target_frame_metadata(md: Dict[str, object], img_w: int, eps: float = 1e-6):
    62	    """Rotate one sample's conditioning into the target-aligned frame.
    63	
    64	    phi_ref = reference_azimuth(md); None -> return dict(md) unchanged (shallow
    65	    copy, matching rotate_scene_metadata's no-mutation contract).
    66	    Otherwise: rotate_scene_metadata(md, -phi_ref, img_w)  — depth + all four
    67	    pose keys, column-quantized, caller's dict never mutated.
    68	    img_w comes from the caller (metadata[0]['depth'].shape[-1] upstream);
    69	    if 'depth' is absent the poses still rotate (rotate_scene_metadata already
    70	    handles a depth-less dict) — quantization then still uses img_w so train
    71	    and any depth-less eval agree.
    72	    """
    73	    ...
    74	```
