./CLAUDE.md:148:**⚠️ Eval-protocol flags are part of the experiment, not defaults.** `eval_FLAC.py` takes `--cond-method {vanilla,fa_invariant}` (plus `--frame-avg-angles`, `--rotate-deg`/`--rotate-mode` for C₄ sweeps and the 45° negative control, `--cond-autocast {default,bf16,off}`). **`--cond-autocast bf16` is part of the registered table protocol** (`model_comparison.md` line 4) and the CLI default is `default`, NOT bf16 — omitting it makes numbers incomparable to every existing row (caught by Codex on exp_17's 128-cell grid before launch). `eval_FLAC.py` also **writes its metric JSON to `dirname(--ckpt-path)`** — never point it at another checkout's checkpoints in place; symlink them into your own outputs tree first (pattern: `exp_17…/yaw_aug_a6000_roteval_run.sh`). **The flag must match how the checkpoint was trained.** A mismatch produces plausible-looking but catastrophically wrong numbers in both directions — the fa-trained B-F@40k reads `8.202/0.978/38.79/R5.39` under fa eval and `10.652/2.082/80.86/R0.68` under vanilla eval. Evaluating fa checkpoints with the default (vanilla) conditioning caused exp_09's protocol error and one retracted exp_07 conclusion. **Put the eval-protocol flags in every launch/screen manifest; never rely on the default.**
